From c46634ab0fbb56049e4d44854bcc559a84922059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Pelenitsyn <a.pelenitsyn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:35:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Accept every extension and re-exported modules with mhs

mhs has the extensions it implements always on, CPP excepted, and ignores
the LANGUAGE pragmas of the others. Describing only the extensions it
implements made Cabal reject packages for extensions they merely declare,
often for the GHC side of a conditional: Trustworthy (parsec), DeriveGeneric
(pretty), UnboxedTuples (unordered-containers, vault), UnliftedFFITypes
(psqueues, these), TypeFamilies (newtype, contravariant, assoc), or
NoGeneralizedNewtypeDeriving, for which the solver fell back from time-1.15,
which supports mhs, to time-1.12.2. Describe every extension as supported,
as MicroCabal effectively does by not checking them: a package that needs an
extension mhs lacks fails when mhs meets the syntax.

mhs sees all the modules of the packages it loads, which include the
dependencies of the dependencies of a component, so the modules a package
re-exports are visible to the components depending on it, as long as they
are not renamed. Configure no longer rejects packages with
reexported-modules, such as ansi-terminal, with mhs.

Measured by building, one at a time with cabal and mhs 0.16.9.0, the 91
packages of MicroHs's Makefile.packages, the list its hackage-ci workflow
installs with mcabal: 39 built before, 42 after, and the solver rejects none
of them anymore. Of the other 49, 36 fail on the missing version macros
(transformers alone blocks 23) and 11 on the implicit ghc-compat dependency
that mcabal adds to every package.

