-      , TypeOperators
-      , TypeSynonymInstances
-      , UndecidableInstances
-      , UndecidableSuperClasses
-      , UnicodeSyntax
-      , ViewPatterns
-      ]
-    -- NoDatatypeContexts and NoStarIsType
-    alwaysOff = [DatatypeContexts, StarIsType]
     -- Extensions of MicroHs that GHC does not have.
     mhsSpecific = ["ExtraInstanceBindings", "ImportShadowing", "TypeLits"]
 
diff --git a/changelog.d/pr-11392.md b/changelog.d/pr-11392.md
index 9669a88fb..c26959c72 100644
--- a/changelog.d/pr-11392.md
+++ b/changelog.d/pr-11392.md
@@ -22,3 +22,8 @@ The `base` of mhs is versioned like mhs itself and bundles the modules of
 `integer-logarithms`. So that packages written for GHC solve, Cabal presents it
 as `base-4.19.1.0` and the bundled packages as installed packages of their
 own, at the versions MicroCabal uses for the same purpose.
+
+Since mhs ignores the `LANGUAGE` pragmas of the extensions it does not
+implement, packages are not rejected for the extensions they declare, and
+`reexported-modules` are accepted, as mhs sees all the modules of the
+packages it loads.
